<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moutier-Grandval Abbey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moutier-Grandval Abbey was a monastery founded around 640 at Moutier in the Jura mountains of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. In 999 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-iii-of-burgundy">Rudolf III of Burgundy</a> gave it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Basel, forming the core of the prince-bishopric's lands in the Jura. Its chapter moved to Delémont after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, and its Carolingian Moutier-Grandval Bible is in the British Library.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moutier-grandval-abbey.jpg" alt="Moutier-Grandval Abbey" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E. Käppelin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruins_of_the_Moutier_Abbey,_circa_1830s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
